{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1171 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "15d542fcbb4f7aa3d499250ce1b852f49a4db082f4e16488549189a056657a1a" :edb/db-before-t 1170 :edb/db-after-t 1171 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534483 50 #inst "2026-10-07T07:59:29.544Z" 13194139534483 true] [17592186064093 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291382 13194139534483 true] [17592186068623 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291396 13194139534483 true] [17592186083068 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291410 13194139534483 true] [17592186083149 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291417 13194139534483 true] [17592186083227 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291375 13194139534483 true] [17592186083824 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534483 true] [17592186083824 1100 "For the parametric curve\n\n$x = 3\\sin \\theta , y = 5\\cos \\theta , 0 \\le \\theta  < 2\\pi $, calculate $\\frac{dy}{dx}$." 13194139534483 false] [17592186083824 1100 "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,\n$$\n\n calculate $\\frac{dy}{dx}.$" 13194139534483 true] [17592186083824 1145 "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(\\theta )}{{x}^{′}(\\theta )}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(\\theta )=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,{y}^{′}(\\theta )=-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }=-\\frac{5}{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta .\n$$" 13194139534483 true] [17592186083902 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534483 true] [17592186083902 1100 "Solve the equation $\\frac{1}{S + 1} + \\frac{2}{S - 1} = \\frac{1}{S^{2} - 1}$." 13194139534483 false] [17592186083902 1100 "Solve the equation $\\frac{1}{S+1}+\\frac{2}{S-1}=\\frac{1}{{S}^{2}-1}.$" 13194139534483 true] [17592186083902 1145 "First, we factor the quadratic denominator, giving us the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{S+1}+\\frac{2}{S-1}=\\frac{1}{(S-1)(S+1)}.\n$$\n\nWe now make the following observations:\n\n- The least common denominator of our equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{LCM}(S-1,\\,S+1,\\,(S-1)(S+1))=(S-1)(S+1).\n$$\n\n- The values $S=1$ and $S=-1$ cannot be solutions to our equation. These values make at least one denominator in our original equation equal zero, and division by zero is undefined.\n\nNow, multiplying both sides of the equation by the least common denominator, we can simplify it as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{S+1}+\\frac{2}{S-1} & =\\frac{1}{(S-1)(S+1)} \\\\ (S-1)(S+1)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{S+1}+\\frac{2}{S-1}) & =(S-1)(S+1)\\cdot \\frac{1}{(S-1)(S+1)} \\\\ \\frac{(S-1)(S+1)}{S+1}+\\frac{2(S-1)(S+1)}{S-1} & =\\frac{(S-1)(S+1)}{(S-1)(S+1)} \\\\ \\frac{(S-1)\\cdot \\cancel{(S+1)}}{\\cancel{S+1}}+\\frac{2(S+1)\\cdot \\cancel{(S-1)}}{\\cancel{S-1}} & =\\frac{\\cancel{(S-1)(S+1)}}{\\cancel{(S-1)(S+1)}} \\\\ S-1+2(S+1) & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this equation for $S,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S-1+2(S+1) & =1 \\\\ S-1+2S+2 & =1 \\\\ 3S & =0 \\\\ S & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $0\\ne 1$ and $0\\ne -1,$ we conclude that $S=0$ is a valid solution. \n\nTherefore, the solution to our original equation is $S=0.$" 13194139534483 true] [17592186087606 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291368 13194139534483 true] [17592186087660 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291361 13194139534483 true] [17592186087685 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291403 13194139534483 true] [17592186110526 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291389 13194139534483 true] [17592186291361 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291362 13194139534483 true] [17592186291361 1089 "q-103912" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291361 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534483 true] [17592186291361 1100 "Write the equation of the hyperbola $2{x}^{2}-9{y}^{2}=18$ in standard form." 13194139534483 true] [17592186291361 1113 #uuid "f2af82f3-9d93-5885-b2ca-b940ebfe011c" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291361 1145 "The Cartesian equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, to write the equation of the hyperbola in standard form, we need to divide both sides of the equation by $18$ and then simplify, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}-9{y}^{2} & =18 \\\\ \\frac{2{x}^{2}}{18}-\\frac{9{y}^{2}}{18} & =\\frac{18}{18} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291362 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291363 13194139534483 true] [17592186291362 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291364 13194139534483 true] [17592186291362 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291365 13194139534483 true] [17592186291362 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291366 13194139534483 true] [17592186291362 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291367 13194139534483 true] [17592186291362 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534483 true] [17592186291362 1041 "selection" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291362 1104 #edb/ref 17592186291366 13194139534483 true] [17592186291362 1110 #uuid "370cd7ad-7240-594d-ad13-7fd0f8b42fe5" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291363 1034 "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291363 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534483 true] [17592186291363 1111 #uuid "0b50fd87-9a94-519a-b2df-b7c7fbd644a8" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291364 1034 "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}=1" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291364 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534483 true] [17592186291364 1111 #uuid "33bd661e-3a94-5a8d-9ad0-ef287e924386" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291365 1034 "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}=1" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291365 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534483 true] [17592186291365 1111 #uuid "c8ad4a90-4398-5697-b748-eb04f4a456fc" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291366 1034 "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}=1" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291366 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534483 true] [17592186291366 1111 #uuid "0119602e-ae05-5631-a3c6-326cf98ca0a0" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291367 1034 "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291367 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534483 true] [17592186291367 1111 #uuid "e7cf1c64-d8e0-50ff-83cd-f5b85bd3fdcc" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291368 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291369 13194139534483 true] [17592186291368 1089 "q-120347" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291368 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534483 true] [17592186291368 1100 "Express $2{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})-2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})$ as a single trigonometric ratio." 13194139534483 true] [17592186291368 1113 #uuid "3e51393b-cf1d-5d4b-917b-3f067d1f544f" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291368 1145 "Our expression can be factored as follows:\n\n$$\n2({cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})-{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}))\n$$\n\nNow, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})-{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2({cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})-{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})) & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291369 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291370 13194139534483 true] [17592186291369 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291371 13194139534483 true] [17592186291369 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291372 13194139534483 true] [17592186291369 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291373 13194139534483 true] [17592186291369 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291374 13194139534483 true] [17592186291369 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534483 true] [17592186291369 1041 "selection" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291369 1104 #edb/ref 17592186291370 13194139534483 true] [17592186291369 1110 #uuid "3d960efe-ceb6-58e1-832b-78da060375a8" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291370 1034 "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291370 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534483 true] [17592186291370 1111 #uuid "f1c71444-dd4a-57b1-96b8-200c7235140d" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291371 1034 "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291371 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534483 true] [17592186291371 1111 #uuid "398dfc9d-8215-548e-8963-d32de0b78d79" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291372 1034 "4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291372 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534483 true] [17592186291372 1111 #uuid "36a888a2-9999-59ec-9cd8-229ed3030d6a" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291373 1034 "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291373 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534483 true] [17592186291373 1111 #uuid "afbd5857-1419-532c-abc1-5c27e3bea386" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291374 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291374 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534483 true] [17592186291374 1111 #uuid "3c8024b9-98a7-5742-8975-44f2db7f5d5c" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291375 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291376 13194139534483 true] [17592186291375 1089 "q-122298" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291375 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534483 true] [17592186291375 1100 "In box $A,$ there are $7$ red marbles and $3$ green marbles. In box $B,$ there are $2$ red marbles and $8$ green marbles. If we randomly select one of the boxes and then we randomly select one marble from that box, what is the probability that it’s a green marble?" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291375 1113 #uuid "490c0980-5ac4-561f-af02-cd8ffe3a3650" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291375 1142 true 13194139534483 true] [17592186291375 1145 "Let $G$ be the event that a green marble is selected, and let $A$ be the event that box $A$ is selected. Then ${A}^{′}$ is the event that box $B$ is selected. \n\nTo calculate the probability that a selected marble is green, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(G)=P(G|A)P(A)+P(G|{A}^{′})P({A}^{′})\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each bit of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since there are $2$ boxes, we have\n\n$$\nP(A)=\\frac{1}{2},\\,P({A}^{′})=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\n- Since there are $3$ green marbles of the total of $10$ marbles in box $A$ and $8$  green marbles of the total of $10$ marbles in box $B,$ we have\n\n$$\nP(G|A)=\\frac{3}{10},\\,P(G|{A}^{′})=\\frac{8}{10}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a selected marble is green is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(G) & =P(G|A)P(A)+P(G|{A}^{′})P({A}^{′}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{3}{10})(\\frac{1}{2})+(\\frac{8}{10})(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{20}+\\frac{8}{20} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291376 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291377 13194139534483 true] [17592186291376 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291378 13194139534483 true] [17592186291376 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291379 13194139534483 true] [17592186291376 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291380 13194139534483 true] [17592186291376 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291381 13194139534483 true] [17592186291376 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534483 true] [17592186291376 1041 "selection" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291376 1104 #edb/ref 17592186291380 13194139534483 true] [17592186291376 1110 #uuid "edc192ef-45f1-53c0-98e5-8cc69d753029" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291377 1034 "\\frac{2}{3}" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291377 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534483 true] [17592186291377 1111 #uuid "28822b93-4c9d-5cc5-aab7-f110c323de0a" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291378 1034 "\\frac{3}{5}" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291378 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534483 true] [17592186291378 1111 #uuid "c16212fb-8f3a-52ce-83aa-03b289b43dbb" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291379 1034 "\\frac{1}{5}" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291379 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534483 true] [17592186291379 1111 #uuid "420d6e97-d13a-5227-b04d-1808fae2deae" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291380 1034 "\\frac{11}{20}" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291380 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534483 true] [17592186291380 1111 #uuid "e1b19b9e-fb87-54ad-a6d2-fce696977322" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291381 1034 "\\frac{1}{3}" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291381 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534483 true] [17592186291381 1111 #uuid "748616c3-4625-57a9-b33a-1e6c83d856f1" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291382 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291383 13194139534483 true] [17592186291382 1089 "q-2281" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291382 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534483 true] [17592186291382 1100 "$\\int ({9}^{x}+3{e}^{x})\\,\\text{d}x=$" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291382 1113 #uuid "0ac5a63d-ba5d-5b91-87a0-a208698bb5b6" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291382 1145 "Here, we combine the sum rule and our exponential rules to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int ({9}^{x}+3{e}^{x})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {9}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x+3\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{9}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡9}+3{e}^{x}+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291383 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291384 13194139534483 true] [17592186291383 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291385 13194139534483 true] [17592186291383 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291386 13194139534483 true] [17592186291383 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291387 13194139534483 true] [17592186291383 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291388 13194139534483 true] [17592186291383 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534483 true] [17592186291383 1041 "selection" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291383 1104 #edb/ref 17592186291385 13194139534483 true] [17592186291383 1110 #uuid "48f6d1ae-18fd-535a-9588-2fec5296aec0" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291384 1034 "\\frac{{x}^{9}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡9}-3{e}^{x}+C" 13194139534483 true] [17592186291384 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534483 true] [17592186291384 1111 #uuid "d877fa7e-da62-5607-8a68-7a6113b8b1f6" 131